3.—(1) For the purposes of section 16(1)(b) of the Act, the amount of cash grant to be payable to a Pioneer with disability is $100 every month, if the Pioneer satisfies the condition in paragraph (2).
(2) The Pioneer may be paid the cash grant under paragraph (1) if, in relation to the Pioneer’s substantial need for continuing support in activities of daily living, the Pioneer requires permanent support from any person in carrying out at least 3 of the following activities of daily living:
(a)walking or moving on any level surface;
(b)dressing;
(c)washing or bathing;
(d)feeding oneself food;
(e)transferring from a chair to a bed, or vice versa;
(f)toileting.
